[38;2;124;124;124m6. Since closed geodesics are dense in T¹(f(S)) and F is continuous, F = 0 [0m
[38;2;124;124;124meverywhere.[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m7. F = 0 everywhere means II = 0, so f(S) is totally geodesic.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mTherefore, YES, we can conclude f(S) is totally geodesic.[0m

